# Deploy = SHIP EVERYTHING

When the user says **Deploy**, **ship**, **go live**, or **ship everything** on DESKTOP:

## Mandatory command

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/ship-everything.ps1 -Message "concise commit message"
```

- If the working tree already has **no shippable uncommitted changes**, omit `-Message`:
  ```powershell
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/ship-everything.ps1
  ```
- Do **not** run bare `firebase deploy` alone for a user "Deploy" request.
- Do **not** `git push` without ensuring a commit happened first for any pending code.
- Do **not** leave uncommitted HTML/CSS/JS/functions on disk while pushing or deploying — that caused the 2026-07-20 ping-pong (live ≠ GitHub).

## What the script guarantees

1. Commit all shippable dirty files (ignores `.firebase/` cache and secret key files)
2. `git push` so `HEAD` == `origin/main`
3. `firebase deploy` for detected targets (hosting / functions / rules)
4. Abort if local is behind remote, or if git drifts after push

## Forbidden

- Saying "Deployed" after only `git commit` or only `git push`
- Manual `firebase deploy` while shippable files are still uncommitted
- Assuming GitHub Actions will "catch up" uncommitted disk edits (it will not — CI deploys **committed** files only)

## After success

One line to user: **Deployed — live on https://gisugo.com now.** (git + Firebase synced)

## Cloud Agent exception

If `firebase --version` is unavailable: PR → squash-merge (CI deploys). Never claim desktop Firebase deploy from Cloud.
